Learn the lesson: Do not waste your time lashing out in all directions at what seems to be a many-headed enemy. Find the one head that matters, the person with willpower, or msarts, or ,most important of all, Charisma.

Whatever it costs you, lure this person away, for once his powers will lose their effect. 
His isolation can be physical(banishment or absence from the court), poltical (narrowing his base of support), or psychological (alientating hom from the group through slander and insinutaiton). Cnaer begins with a single cell, excise before it spreads beyond cure. 

Keys to Power: People will congreagate around a single storng peronsality like planets orbitting a sun. 

Dr. Milton H. Erickson

In the game of Chess you try to isolate the king but in the game of Go you try to isolate the enemy's forces in small pockets, rendering them immobile and ineffectual. 

It is often better to isolate your enemies than to destroy them-you seem less brutal. 

When Mao Tse-tung wanted to eliminate an enemy int he ruling eleite, he did not confront the person directly, he silently, and steathily worked to islate the man, divide his allies, and turn them away from him, shrink his support. 

Queen Elizabeth's prime minister Robert Cecil sent his main rivals away to do his plotting: the Earl of Essex and Sir Walter Raleigh. 

First, your absence form the court spells danger for you and you should never leave the scene of utrmoil, for your abscence can both symbolize and induce a lose power; second, and on the other hand lurign your enemies away from the court at critical moments is a gerat ploy. 

The monk Rasoutin gained his power ocer Czar Nicholas and Czar Alexandra of Russia because they were isolated from the common folk.

Hernando Corts and Fransisco Pizarro took kings Moctezum and Atahualpa to allow the kingdom to fall into turmoil. 

Reversal: Any harm you do to   man should be done in such a way that you need not fear his revenge. Andrew Johnson made Ulysses S. Grant his enemy by isolating him but this enraged Ulysses which paved the way for him trying to and becoming president. 

