Law 32: Play to People's fantasies 

Cypriot Mamugna AKA Il Bragadino

The Reality: Change is slow and gradual. It requires hard work, a bit of luck, a fair amount of self-sacrifice, and a lot of patience. 
Fantasy: A sudden transformation will bring a total change in one's fortunes, bypassing work, luck, self-sacrafice, and time in one fantastic stroke. 

Leonard Thurneisser

The Reality: The social realm has hard-set codes and boundaries. We understand these limits and know that we have to within the same familiar circles, day in and day out.  
Fantasy: We can enter a totally new world with different codes and the promise of adventure. 

George Psalmanazar (embellished Taiwan known as Formosa during his time) 
Dancer Mata Hari

The Reality: Society is fragmented and full of conflict
The Fantasy: People can come together in a mystical union of souls

Oscar Hartzell

The Reality: The dead cannot be brought back to life, the past cannot be changed
Fantasy: A sudden reversal of this fact

Dutch Forgerer: Han Ver Meegeren

Reversal: Lincoln(Lawyer with a beard, becomes the common-man lawyer)
Tom Thumb


